.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt MAGSAFE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm magsafe
.Nd control the light on an Apple MagSafe 3 cable
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl n
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Nm
.Fl h | -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
controls the light on Apple's USB-C to MagSafe 3 cable (A2363) and reads the
cable's firmware state.
Color comes from the Mac's SMC; brightness and diagnostics come from fixed
messages to the cable.
It changes only the cable's RAM brightness and the Mac's light color setting,
never firmware or stored calibration.
.Pp
Commands that touch hardware run
.Nm
again through
.Xr sudo 8 ,
which may ask for a password, unless the daemon is installed: then the daemon
runs them without one.
Only one such command can run at a time.
Every reset, including the one at the end of each effect, returns the light to
the saved settings.
Options can appear before or after the command.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm status
Show the firmware version, security flags, and light state.
.It Cm reset
Set both brightness scales and the color mode to the saved settings: 100% and
color control by macOS unless changed with
.Cm settings .
Every step is attempted even if another fails.
.It Cm led set Ar mode
Set the light to
.Cm auto ,
.Cm off ,
.Cm green ,
or
.Cm amber .
.Cm auto
does not change brightness.
.It Cm led brightness Ar color percent
Light
.Cm green
or
.Cm amber
at 0 to 100% brightness, then wait up to 2 seconds for the cable's PWM output
to match.
.It Cm led blink Ar color
Switch between 100% and 0%, once per interval.
.Ar color
is
.Cm green ,
.Cm amber ,
or
.Cm alternate .
.It Cm led fade-in Ar color
Ramp up, switch off, then stay dark for the interval.
.It Cm led fade-out Ar color
Switch on, ramp down, then stay dark for the interval.
.It Cm led fade Ar color
Ramp up, ramp down, then stay dark for the interval.
.It Cm led stream Ar color
Light
.Cm green
or
.Cm amber
at the brightness percentages read from standard input, one per line, until
the input ends.
Spaces around a number are allowed and blank lines are skipped.
Only the newest value is used, at most 40 times a second, and the color is
checked every 5 seconds.
.It Cm timer Ar duration
Count down on the light.
It lights green and dims as time runs out, switches to amber for the last fifth
of the time, at most 5 minutes, then flashes amber until interrupted or for
.Fl -count
flashes.
.Ar duration
is 10 seconds to 24 hours, such as
.Cm 25m ,
.Cm 90s ,
or
.Cm 1h30m ;
a plain number is minutes.
Interrupting the alarm exits with 0; interrupting the countdown exits as an
effect does.
.It Cm morse Ar text ...
Send text in green, in international Morse code.
A dot lasts one unit and a dash three; the light is dark for one unit within a
character, three between characters, and seven between words and repetitions.
The unit is
.Fl -interval-ms ,
150 ms by default.
Text may have up to 200 letters, digits, and the punctuation
.Li ". , ? ' ! / ( ) & : ; = + - _ \(dq $ @" .
Morse code repeats until interrupted unless
.Fl -count
is given.
.It Cm settings
Show the saved brightness and color mode.
.It Cm settings dim Ar percent
Save the brightness, 0 to 100, that the light returns to, and apply it.
.It Cm settings color Ar mode
Save the color mode,
.Cm auto ,
.Cm off ,
.Cm green ,
or
.Cm amber ,
that the light returns to, and apply it.
.It Cm settings reset
Return to 100% brightness and color control by macOS.
.It Cm daemon install
Copy
.Nm
to a root-owned path, and start it as a launchd daemon that runs commands
without a password for root, the user at the screen, and admins.
The daemon applies the saved settings again at boot, on plug-in, and on wake.
Run it again after upgrading
.Nm ;
until then, commands use
.Xr sudo 8 .
.It Cm daemon uninstall
Stop and remove the daemon.
.It Cm daemon status
Show whether the daemon is installed and running, and its version.
.It Cm led get
Show the light mode, the two PWM outputs, and the color selector.
.It Cm firmware version
Show the cable firmware version.
.It Cm firmware security
Show the configuration-setter lock and signature-skip flags.
.It Cm firmware calibration
Show the four stored light calibration values.
.It Cm visualizer Op Ar color
Pulse
.Cm green
(the default) or
.Cm amber
to whatever the Mac is playing, until interrupted.
The light flashes with the kick drum and falls to a dim glow between kicks,
even in loud, heavily limited songs.
Beats are sharp rises in the bass that stand out from the song's own recent
rises.
When the beats follow a steady tempo with a kick on nearly every beat, hits
between the kicks flash dimmer.
Audio capture and analysis run as the invoking user; only
.Cm led stream
runs through
.Xr sudo 8 .
Requires macOS 14.2 or later and System Audio Recording permission for the
terminal app.
.It Cm capabilities
List supported and unavailable functions.
.It Cm version
Show the
.Nm
version.
.It Cm help
Show a usage summary.
.El
.Pp
Blink and fade effects repeat until interrupted unless
.Fl -count
is given.
They select their color while dark, wait 450 ms for the cable's own color
transition, and end with
.Cm reset
on completion, error, or
.Dv SIGINT ,
.Dv SIGTERM ,
or
.Dv SIGHUP .
Fades check the PWM output at the top and bottom of every cycle.
Streams and the visualizer prepare their color the same way and also end with
.Cm reset .
.Pp
Diagnostics, brightness, and effects require cable firmware 3.2.0.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -json
Print the result, or the error, as one JSON object on standard output.
Commands that change the light print nothing on success without this option.
.It Fl n , Fl -dry-run
Check the command and print its plan without touching hardware or asking for a
password.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show a usage summary.
.It Fl -version
Show the version.
.It Fl c , Fl -count Ar n
Number of blink or fade cycles, timer alarm flashes, or Morse repetitions: 1 to
300, or
.Cm infinite
(the default).
A finite effect or alarm must be planned to take 60 seconds or less.
.It Fl i , Fl -interval-ms Ar ms
Blink or timer alarm on and off time, dark time after each fade cycle, or Morse
dot time: 100 to 10000 (default 500, or 150 for Morse code).
.It Fl d , Fl -duration-ms Ar ms
Time for each fade ramp: 500 to 60000 (default 1000).
.It Fl -preview
Visualizer only: draw the levels on standard error instead of driving the
light, without the cable or
.Xr sudo 8 .
When standard error is not a terminal, print one percentage per line.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev MAGSAFE_NO_DAEMON
If set, use
.Xr sudo 8
even when the daemon is installed.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/run/magsafe-cli.lock
Lock held while a hardware command runs.
.It Pa "/Library/Application Support/magsafe/settings"
The saved settings.
.It Pa /Library/PrivilegedHelperTools/com.mpopv.magsafe
The daemon's root-owned copy of
.Nm .
.It Pa /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.mpopv.magsafe.plist
The daemon's launchd job.
.It Pa /var/run/magsafe.sock
The daemon's socket.
.It Pa /Library/Logs/magsafe-daemon.log
The daemon's log.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success, including a timer alarm that was interrupted.
.It 1
Device, permission, or lock error.
.It 2
Invalid command, option, or value, including an invalid
.Cm led stream
line.
.It 128 + Ar n
An effect, stream, visualizer, or timer countdown stopped by signal
.Ar n ,
such as 130 for Ctrl-C.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Set a dim green light:
.Dl $ magsafe led brightness green 25
.Pp
Alternate green and amber six times, 250 ms each way:
.Dl $ magsafe led blink alternate -c 6 -i 250
.Pp
Fade amber up and down until Ctrl-C:
.Dl $ magsafe led fade amber
.Pp
Pulse amber to the music until Ctrl-C:
.Dl $ magsafe visualizer amber
.Pp
Run a 25-minute timer:
.Dl $ magsafe timer 25m
.Pp
Send SOS three times:
.Dl $ magsafe morse sos -c 3
.Pp
Check audio capture without the cable:
.Dl $ magsafe visualizer --preview
.Pp
Ramp green up over 2 seconds from a script:
.Dl $ for p in $(seq 0 5 100); do echo $p; sleep 0.1; done | magsafe led stream green
.Pp
Show the plan of an effect as JSON, without touching hardware:
.Dl $ magsafe --json --dry-run led fade-in green -c 3 -d 2000
.Pp
Keep the light dim, and apply that at every plug-in:
.Dl $ magsafe settings dim 10
.Dl $ sudo magsafe daemon install
.Pp
Return the light to the saved settings:
.Dl $ magsafe reset
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr launchctl 1 ,
.Xr sudo 8
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/mpopv/magsafe-cli
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
uses private Apple interfaces and has been tested on one Mac with one cable
firmware version.
.Pp
macOS keeps System Audio Recording permission per app, and for
.Nm
that app is the terminal.
macOS asks for it the first time
.Cm visualizer
runs.
If it was denied, or the terminal app gets no prompt, allow the app, or add it
under System Audio Recording Only, in System Settings > Privacy & Security >
Screen & System Audio Recording.
